## Context-retry carry-over note

During sandbox verification, an earlier context-retry mock-style path showed a mismatch around fallback context bounds. Michael's local tests passed, and the mismatch appeared to be reproducible against the baseline reference in the sandbox, so it was not treated as a drain-shutdown regression.

The important condition preserved for future review:

```text
Context creation retry must not increase context memory pressure relative to the failed base createContext attempt.
```

More specifically:

```text
If the failed base attempt used a fixed or bounded context size, retry fallback bounds should be capped by the base attempt's context bounds.
```

Do not change context retry logic in this branch unless current local/current-contract tests reproduce an issue.

## Known warnings / non-issues

### JSON module warning

Real runtime tests may print:

```text
ExperimentalWarning: Importing JSON modules is an experimental feature and might change at any time
```

This warning appeared during local real-runtime testing and did not fail the smoke run.

### Line endings

Some source files in the reference package used CRLF line endings, while staged/generated files may use LF. This can produce diff noise but is not a logic issue.

